"length":"1692.57","height":"0","width":"0"},{"name":"radia_s28_n373_reboot_timemachine_ufos-2-Final.png","source":"derivative","format":"PNG","original":"radia_s28_n373_reboot_timemachine_ufos-2-Final.mp3","mtime":"1493876241","size":"9483","md5":"00bb6e44f962400cd6ef021926dad8b3","crc32":"cc7c9997","sha1":"0e3c6ff9108f8daa95b1ea1c01677e0b2cde1dde"},{"name":"radia_s28_n373_reboot_timemachine_ufos_archive.torrent","source":"metadata","btih":"3bd8563f6d973027fa5baf37e18fd11647f5adcd","mtime":"1553296361","size":"6351","md5":"11bd2bfc4d9db27d78cc74832856c06b","crc32":"ec44ac9d","sha1":"c04b83b83e588652484b4ccdda0353550ba0814a","format":"Archive BitTorrent"},{"name":"radia_s28_n373_reboot_timemachine_ufos_files.xml","source":"original","format":"Metadata","md5":"8c35bac9c1b67bc645a73876350d0204","summation":"md5"},{"name":"radia_s28_n373_reboot_timemachine_ufos_meta.sqlite","source":"original","mtime":"1493876039","size":"18432","format":"Metadata","md5":"73116cffb5874451ac93f21587d54552","crc32":"ba1336a0","sha1":"fa832294ddeaa2d57d54088159e232849ba6abe4"},{"name":"radia_s28_n373_reboot_timemachine_ufos_meta.xml","source":"original","mtime":"1726476541","size":"1905","format":"Metadata","md5":"ee50e1bf22ad115f5d6f7c6e13ad938f","crc32":"aee323a2","sha1":"6fe86c078ea9d84c65ec85431d4b4dabd79a521b"}],"files_count":11,"item_last_updated":1726476541,"item_size":87139848,"metadata":{"identifier":"radia_s28_n373_reboot_timemachine_ufos","mediatype":"audio","collection":["radiafm","radioprograms","radiostationarchives"],"description":"<div class=\"entry-content\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Between live mix, sound collage and scientific experiment, “The\n Time Machine” explores the many dimensions of past and present day \nelectronic dance music, quantum-jumping the barriers within the genre, \nblurring the lines between past, present and future, with its \nsearch-lights focused on the rare and unusual.</p>\n<p>The test-pilot is Daze Dasen aka Plastique de Rêve, a swiss deejay \nand producer with releases on labels such as Gigolo, Turbo, DFA, \nSupersoul Recordings, Mental Groove or Space Factory Disques. Originally\n from Geneva but now a long-time Berlin resident, Plastique De Rêve’s \nfascination for electronic sounds goes back to his childhood in the 70s,\n and he has studied, produced and collected electronic music since 1984 \nup to this day.</p>\n<p>http://listn.to/PlastiqueDeReve</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>","licenseurl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/3.0/","radiaseason":"28","scanner":"Internet Archive HTML5 Uploader 1.6.3","subject":"radio art;Radia;Reboot.fm","title":"Show 0373: THE TIME MACHINE - Ufos by Plastique de Rêve (Reboot.fm)","publicdate":"2017-05-04 05:32:59","uploader":"radia.fm@gmail.com","addeddate":"2017-05-04 05:32:59","date":"2012-05-21","creator":"Reboot.fm","backup_location":"ia906403_17","external_metadata_update":"2019-03-22T23:12:14Z","collection_added":"radiostationarchives"},"server":"ia803403.us.archive.org","uniq":1326231299,"workable_servers":["ia803403.us.archive.org","ia903403.us.archive.org"]}